  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The rotary axis fit refuses a model that is not a shape of revolution. The refusal text now names the 4-axis case.\n- New text: \"the model's normals share no rotation axis - it is not a shape of revolution, and the rotary kinds need one today; 4-axis work on a part clamped on A that is not turned (helical lobes, a carving) is not supported yet (#2772); on a 5-axis machine, finish a freeform with the 5-Axis kinds\".\n- The words \"share no rotation axis\" stay. Existing tests and callers that match on them do not change.\n- The `RotaryContour` doc comment in `params.rs` now describes the new refusal.\n- The decision file is `docs/decisions/2772-rotary-4axis-refusal.md`.\n\nThis PR is the first slice of #2772 (item 3 of \"Wanted\"). It does not close the issue.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe old refusal pointed only at the 5-Axis kinds. The reporter has a 4-axis machine. The message gave this user no correct next step.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pin: `multiaxis::axis_consensus::tests::the_freeform_refusal_names_the_4_axis_case` (motion lib).\n- Red before the fix: yes. The failure printed the old text.\n- Mutation: the old string put back gives red. The new string gives green.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 34 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No posted G-code or CL output changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full feature of #2772 is not in this PR. These parts stay open for later PRs:\n  - a stated rotary axis, with a refusal when it and the turned faces disagree;\n  - the same axis for each consumer that now fits it again from the mesh;\n  - a radial drop finish and radial-step roughing.\n- The decision file gives the reasons for the split.\n- The UI shows the refusal text as it is. No UI test was run for this text.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes these files.\n\nChangelog: A rotary operation on a part that is not a shape of revolution now says that 4-axis work on such a part is not supported yet (#2772), not only that it needs the 5-Axis kinds.\n\nRefs #2772\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
